[9] The RPD found the determinative issue to be IFA. The Appellant was asked whether she can relocate to Bulawayo to avoid her husband. She indicated that she cannot do so for the following reasons:
a. Fears that her husband and his friends will kill her or continue to abuse her;
b. There are relatives all over Zimbabwe that would disclose her location;
c. Her husband has family in Bulawayo, and she fears they would disclose her location;
d. Her husband is politically connected, and she fears he will use this to locate her;
e. Fear that in her communications with her children, they could disclose her location to her husband;
f. The Appellant wishes to file for divorce from her husband and she fears he will know her location through this process, as this requires her to go to court;
g. There are limits to women's freedom of movement, due to the economic and political situation, both locally and nationally, there are regular checkpoints along routes. She fears she will be identified and located.

[10] The test for IFA is two-fold; that there is no serious possibility of persecution in the proposed IFA and conditions in the proposed IFA must be such that it would not be unreasonable to move there, considering the specific needs of the claimant (Appellant).

